<title>SINGAPORE: Bangchak awards 1.0 mln bbls Oman crude in tender.</title>
<headline>Bangchak awards 1.0 mln bbls Oman crude in tender.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Bangchak Petroleum Plc has awarded one million barrels of Oman crude to a Japanese trader in its December buying tender, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>One source said the award was made at a single digit premium to MPM.</p>
<p>Bangchak did not award any Tapis crude, the sources said.</p>
<p>Bangchak had tendered to buy 500,000 barrels of Gulf grade crude and 600,000 barrels of Far East light sweet crudes.  </p>
<p>The refinery bought one cargo of Oman crude in its November tender at MPM flat and 600,000 barrels of Tapis at a premium of $1.15.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
